<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office"
      xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>SmartERP User & Role-Based Flow Documentation</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.6;
            color: #333333;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        h1 {
            color: #1e3a8a;
            font-size: 28pt;
            border-bottom: 2px solid #3b82f6;
            padding-bottom: 5px;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }
        h2 {
            color: #1e40af;
            font-size: 20pt;
            margin-top: 30px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #93c5fd;
            padding-bottom: 3px;
        }
        h3 {
            color: #2563eb;
            font-size: 14pt;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }
        p, li {
            font-size: 11pt;
        }
        table {
            border-collapse: collapse;
            width: 100%;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        th, td {
            border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
            padding: 8px 12px;
            text-align: left;
            font-size: 10.5pt;
        }
        th {
            background-color: #eff6ff;
            color: #1e3a8a;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
        .img-container {
            margin: 20px 0;
            text-align: center;
        }
        img {
            max-width: 100%;
            height: auto;
            border: 1px solid #93c5fd;
        }
        .role-badge {
            display: inline-block;
            background-color: #dbeafe;
            color: #1e40af;
            padding: 2px 6px;
            border-radius: 4px;
            font-size: 9.5pt;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
        .toc {
            background-color: #f9fafb;
            border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
            padding: 15px 20px;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }
        .toc ul {
            list-style-type: none;
            padding-left: 0;
        }
        .toc li {
            margin-bottom: 6px;
        }
        .toc a {
            color: #2563eb;
            text-decoration: none;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>SmartERP System User & Role-Based Flow Manual</h1>
    <p><strong>Prepared for:</strong> Client Handover & Training</p>
    <p><strong>System URL:</strong> http://localhost:5013</p>
    <p>This document provides a comprehensive operational guide for the SmartERP system, including authentication, visual screens, and role-based permissions defining exactly <em>who</em> does <em>what</em> work on <em>which</em> page.</p>

    <div class="toc">
        <h2>Table of Contents</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>1. <a href="#roles-matrix">Role Access & Permission Matrix</a></li>
            <li>2. <a href="#auth-flow">Authentication & Login Flows</a></li>
            <li>3. <a href="#dashboard">Operational Dashboard</a></li>
            <li>4. <a href="#masters">Master Configurations (Setup Data)</a></li>
            <li>5. <a href="#sales">Sales and Billing Cycle</a></li>
            <li>6. <a href="#purchase">Purchase and Procurement Cycle</a></li>
            <li>7. <a href="#inventory">Inventory Control & Warehouse Management</a></li>
            <li>8. <a href="#accounting">Bookkeeping & Double-Entry Vouchers</a></li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <hr/>

    <h2 id="roles-matrix">1. Role Access & Permission Matrix</h2>
    <p>The system features Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) to ensure security and division of labor. Below is the operational matrix mapping user roles to system responsibilities:</p>

    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Module</th>
                <th>Super Admin</th>
                <th>Admin</th>
                <th>Sales User</th>
                <th>Purchase User</th>
                <th>Accountant</th>
                <th>Manager</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>System Config & Logs</strong></td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>Read Only</td>
                <td>No Access</td>
                <td>No Access</td>
                <td>No Access</td>
                <td>No Access</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Masters Setup</strong></td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>Read Only</td>
                <td>Read Only</td>
                <td>Read Only</td>
                <td>Read Only</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Sales Billing</strong></td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>Full Access (Write)</td>
                <td>No Access</td>
                <td>Read Only</td>
                <td>Read Only</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Purchase & GRN</strong></td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>No Access</td>
                <td>Full Access (Write)</td>
                <td>Read Only</td>
                <td>Read Only</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Inventory Operations</strong></td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>Read Only</td>
                <td>Read Only</td>
                <td>No Access</td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Accounting Vouchers</strong></td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>No Access</td>
                <td>No Access</td>
                <td>Full Access (Write)</td>
                <td>Read Only</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Financial Reports</strong></td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>No Access</td>
                <td>No Access</td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
                <td>Full Access</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <hr/>

    <h2 id="auth-flow">2. Authentication & Login Flows</h2>
    <p>This flow regulates access to the entire application. Users who are not logged in are automatically redirected here.</p>

    <h3>2.1 Login Form</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access URL:</strong> <code>http://localhost:5013/Account/Login</code></li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">All Users</span></li>
        <li><strong>Step-by-Step Flow:</strong>
            <ol>
                <li>Input username/email (default: <code>admin@smarterp.com</code>).</li>
                <li>Input secure password (default: <code>Admin@123</code>).</li>
                <li>Click **Log In** to verify credentials against ASP.NET Identity database.</li>
            </ol>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_login.png" alt="Login Screen" />
    </div>

    <hr/>

    <h2 id="dashboard">3. Operational Dashboard</h2>
    <p>The landing page for all authenticated users. Display panels customize based on role privileges.</p>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left navigation Menu -> Dashboard</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">All Users</span></li>
        <li><strong>Key Operations:</strong> Review business KPIs, view pending notifications, and open shortcut links.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_dashboard.png" alt="Dashboard Screen" />
    </div>

    <hr/>

    <h2 id="masters">4. Master Configurations (Setup Data)</h2>
    <p>This module sets up database directories before executing transaction files.</p>

    <h3>4.1 Company Profile Setup</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Masters -> Company</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span></li>
        <li><strong>Key Fields:</strong> Company Details, GSTIN, Bank details, Starting invoice number, Company Logo.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_company.png" alt="Company Setup Screen" />
    </div>

    <h3>4.2 Customer Master</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Masters -> Customer</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Sales User</span></li>
        <li><strong>Actions:</strong> Add new customer, edit customer contact details/GSTIN, soft-delete customer profiles.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_customer.png" alt="Customer Directory Screen" />
    </div>

    <h3>4.3 Supplier Master</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Masters -> Supplier</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Purchase User</span></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_supplier.png" alt="Supplier Directory Screen" />
    </div>

    <h3>4.4 Product Master</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Masters -> Product</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span></li>
        <li><strong>Template & Upload Steps:</strong>
            <ol>
                <li>Click **Download Excel Template** to save the pre-configured <code>.xlsx</code> sheet.</li>
                <li>Enter product details (code, pricing, GST, stock limits).</li>
                <li>Click **Bulk Upload** -> select Excel file -> Click **Upload & Import**.</li>
                <li>Category and Brand fields map dynamically. Missing values are auto-created, and existing product codes are updated.</li>
            </ol>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_product.png" alt="Product Catalog Screen" />
    </div>

    <h3>4.5 Category Setup</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Masters -> Category</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span></li>
        <li><strong>Description:</strong> Set up groupings (e.g., Chainsaw, Powertools) to support transaction dropdown filtering.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_category.png" alt="Category Setup Screen" />
    </div>

    <h3>4.6 Brand Setup</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Masters -> Brand</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_brand.png" alt="Brand Setup Screen" />
    </div>

    <h3>4.7 Unit Setup</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Masters -> Unit</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_unit.png" alt="Unit Setup Screen" />
    </div>

    <h3>4.8 Warehouse Locations</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Masters -> Warehouse</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_warehouse.png" alt="Warehouse Setup Screen" />
    </div>

    <h3>4.9 Employee Setup</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Masters -> Employee</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_employee.png" alt="Employee Setup Screen" />
    </div>

    <hr/>

    <h2 id="sales">5. Sales and Billing Cycle</h2>
    <p>This flow governs client invoicing and quotation processes.</p>

    <h3>5.1 Sales Invoice Screen</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Sales -> Invoice</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Sales User</span></li>
        <li><strong>Category-Based Product Selection:</strong>
            <ol>
                <li>Click **New Invoice** or edit an existing one.</li>
                <li>Select a customer.</li>
                <li>Click **Add Row** in the line items table.</li>
                <li>Choose a **Category** (e.g., *Chainsaw*). The adjacent **Product** dropdown instantly filters to display *only* chainsaw products.</li>
                <li>Input quantity. GST, subtotal, and tax amount auto-calculate immediately.</li>
                <li>Save the invoice, then click the **Print** icon to display the clean blue-themed printable invoice.</li>
            </ol>
        </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_sales_invoice.png" alt="Sales Invoice Screen" />
    </div>

    <hr/>

    <h2 id="purchase">6. Purchase and Procurement Cycle</h2>
    <p>This module handles supplier purchase logging and stock entry.</p>

    <h3>6.1 Purchase Invoice Screen</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Purchase -> Invoice</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Purchase User</span></li>
        <li><strong>Description:</strong> Logs stock purchases from suppliers. Category selection filters products here as well, and defaults rate values to purchase prices.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_purchase_invoice.png" alt="Purchase Invoice Screen" />
    </div>

    <hr/>

    <h2 id="inventory">7. Inventory Control & Warehouse Management</h2>
    <p>Handles initial openings, adjustments, and transfer logs between warehouses.</p>

    <h3>7.1 Stock Opening</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Inventory -> Stock Opening</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span></li>
        <li><strong>Description:</strong> Input initial stock quantity counts. Adjusts <code>OpeningStock</code> and sets <code>CurrentStock</code> in the database.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_stock_opening.png" alt="Stock Opening Screen" />
    </div>

    <h3>7.2 Stock Transfer</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Inventory -> Stock Transfer</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Manager</span></li>
        <li><strong>Description:</strong> Record stock transfers from a source warehouse to a destination warehouse. Enforces stock balance verification.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_stock_transfer.png" alt="Stock Transfer Screen" />
    </div>

    <h3>7.3 Stock Adjustment</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Inventory -> Stock Adjustment</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Manager</span></li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_stock_adjustment.png" alt="Stock Adjustment Screen" />
    </div>

    <hr/>

    <h2 id="accounting">8. Bookkeeping & Double-Entry Vouchers</h2>
    <p>Accounting journals, payment receipts, and contra entries.</p>

    <h3>8.1 Contra Voucher Screen</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Access Path:</strong> Left menu -> Accounts -> Contra Voucher</li>
        <li><strong>Responsible Roles:</strong> <span class="role-badge">Super Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Admin</span> <span class="role-badge">Accountant</span></li>
        <li><strong>Operational Logic:</strong> Log bank transfers or deposits. Enforces double-entry balances; if Debit totals do not match Credit totals, saving is rejected.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="img-container">
        <img src="http://smarterp/screenshot_voucher_contra.png" alt="Voucher Contra Screen" />
    </div>

</body>
</html>

